y, efficiency,...&#10;justification: The candidate provides a transferable&#10;abstraction: using degradation-aware probabilistic&#10;optimization to iteratively design durable products under&#10;competing lifecycle constraints. This maps directly onto the&#10;original problem's need for coupled materials-interface-&#10;degradation-l...&#10;abstract: Green manufacturing has become a pressing issue in&#10;recent years, driven by the acknowledgment of its long-term&#10;social and economic benefits, increasing demand for&#10;environmentally friendly products, and expanding regulations.&#10;One of the key approaches to attaining sustainabilit...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 3&#10;domain: chemical_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Multiscale Modeling of Electrochemical Reactions and&#10;Processes&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Multiscale modeling hierarchy linking&#10;atomistic/material properties, interface reactions, mesoscale&#10;transport, and device-level performance', 'Coupled treatment&#10;of electrochemical reaction conditions, ion/electron&#10;transport, and efficiency losses', 'Use of computational&#10;models to propagate degradation mechanisms across scales',&#10;'Holistic performance evaluation under operational and&#10;lifecycle constraints']&#10;combination_plan: Adopt the candidate’s multiscale&#10;electrochemical modeling framework as a co-design scaffold,&#10;connecting material selection and interface stability models&#10;to cell-level transport, efficiency, safety, recyclability,&#10;and lifetime constraints. This would allow simultaneous&#10;optimiz...&#10;justification: The candidate provides a transferable&#10;abstraction: a coupled multiscale modeling structure that&#10;relates local electrochemical reactions and interface&#10;processes to system-level performance. This maps directly onto&#10;the problem’s need for co-design of materials, interfaces,&#10;degra...&#10;abstract: Multiscale Modeling of Electrochemical Reactions and&#10;Processes is a practical guide to multiscale computational&#10;methodologies. It offers a holistic understanding of the&#10;impact of reaction conditions on the overall performance of&#10;electrolyzers, fuel cells, and energy storage de..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#ead1dc;strokeColor=#a64d79;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="11920" width="620" height="1770" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step8_selected_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step8_selected_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step9" value="Step 9 Idea Generation&#10;status: completed&#10;idea_count: 1&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="13790" width="220" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step8_step_step9" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step_step9"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step9_ideas_panel" value="Step 9 Idea Generation + Novelty Check&#10;count: 1&#10;&#10;1. Degradation-Informed Design of Self-Compensating Chloride-&#10;Feedback Interphases for Stable Solid-State Sodium Energy&#10;Storage&#10;novelty_level: medium&#10;motivation: The future of energy storage requires devices that&#10;are not only efficient and high-performing but also safe,&#10;resource-abundant, recyclable, and durable under intermittent&#10;renewable generation. Alternative storage carriers and device&#10;concepts are being explored for this reason, including formate-&#10;based electrochemical storage [Author et al.,&#10;2021](https://openalex.org/W4234705137) and computationally&#10;optimized redox...&#10;methods: 1. Flux-balance and chloride-feedback dimensionless&#10;model: Build a phase-field/continuum model that couples local&#10;sodium deposition flux, chloride migration, interfacial&#10;passivation, electronic leakage, and chemomechanical stress. The&#10;model defines a local flux-balance number F = J_Na_loc /&#10;J_Cl_heal, where J_Na_loc is the local sodium flux at a&#10;protrusion or defect and J_Cl_heal is the chloride-mediated&#10;healing flux. The healing flux is written as J_Cl_heal = -D_Cl&#10;grad(c_Cl) - (D_Cl c_Cl / RT)(z_Cl F grad(phi)...&#10;novelty_justification: Relative to the provided key references,&#10;the closest existing combination is 'Novel Sulfide-Chloride&#10;Solid-State Electrolytes with Tunable Anion Ratio for Highly&#10;Stable Solid-State Sodium-Ion Batteries' paired with 'Leveraging&#10;Neural Networks and Genetic Algorithms to Refine Electrode&#10;Properties in Redox Flow Batteries'. The first reference&#10;supplies the core material platform—sulfide-chloride sodium&#10;solid electrol...&#10;improvement_suggestions: ['Strengthen mechanistic novelty by&#10;deriving the feedback coefficient kappa_fb from a specific&#10;microscopic coupling—such as sodium-flux-induced chlorine&#10;vacancy migration, stress-assisted chloride transport, or redox-&#10;dependent Cl mobility—and by identifying a unique experimental&#10;signature that cannot be reproduced by ordinary diffusion,&#10;electromigration, or current spreading.', 'Introduce a sharper&#10;conceptual invariant, such as an Onsager cross-coupling&#10;coefficient, chloride-healing Damköhler number, or sign-&#10;reversible feedback index, and design the anti-feedback&#10;interphase to invert that index while keeping composition,&#10;thickness, and initial impedance unchanged. This would make the&#10;claim of dynamic self-compensation more distinct from a static&#10;graded-composition effect.']" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="13790" width="680" height="906" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step9_ideas_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step9" target="step9_ideas_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_1" value="Retrieval 1&#10;step: step1&#10;command: search-papers&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 18&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;query_text: techno-economic comparison of grid-scale&#10;energy storage technologies for high renewable power&#10;systems&#10;keywords: [{'text': 'techno economic', 'score': 10},&#10;{'text': 'economic comparison', 'score': 9}, {'text':&#10;'comparison grid', 'score': 8}, {'text': 'grid scale',&#10;'score': 7}, {'text': 'scale energy', 'score': 6}]&#10;source_type: idea_text&#10;top_k: 18&#10;retrieval_mode: hybrid&#10;target_field: Chemistry&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. Hydrogen Storage with Aluminum Formate, ALF:&#10;Experimental, Computational, and Technoeconomic Studies&#10;(2023) [score=0.4868]&#10;Abstract: Long-duration storage of hydrogen is necessary&#10;for coupling renewable H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; with stationary fuel&#10;cell power applications. In this work, aluminum formate&#10;(ALF), which adopts the ReO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;-type structure, is&#10;shown to have remarkable H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; storage&#10;performanc...&#10;&#10;2. Flow Batteries (2010) [score=0.4851]&#10;Abstract: Renewable energy sources including wind and&#10;solar require reliable electrical energy storage systems&#10;because of their intermittent nature. Electrochemical&#10;energy storage devices such as batteries, fuel cells and&#10;flow batteries, and electrochemical capacitors are among&#10;the lead...&#10;&#10;3. Public Transportation Electrification with the Support&#10;of Mobile Energy Storage (2023) [score=0.4848]&#10;Abst